WEBVTT

00:01.270 --> 00:02.350
Oof.

00:07.520 --> 00:08.860
The cotton wrap...

00:09.360 --> 00:10.730
might be a bit loose.

00:11.490 --> 00:13.740
Come on, what are you
takin' your sweet little time—

00:16.780 --> 00:17.950
Oro?

01:49.000 --> 01:53.000
EPISODE 15:
THAT MAN - RAIJUTA

01:55.380 --> 01:57.800
You really show no mercy as always,
that you don't.

01:57.800 --> 02:00.220
What do you mean, "as always"?

02:00.220 --> 02:02.220
Are you heading out for training,
that you are?

02:02.560 --> 02:05.430
Yeah, to the Maekawa Dojo
that I always go to.

02:05.720 --> 02:08.140
That's right! Why don't you
come with me today, Kenshin?

02:08.440 --> 02:12.940
Mr. Maekawa, their master, has been
saying he would love to meet you once.

02:12.940 --> 02:16.240
No, I will pass for now, that I will.

02:16.240 --> 02:18.200
I have to chop some wood and draw a bath.

02:18.450 --> 02:21.570
I see. Then can I ask you to go shopping?

02:21.570 --> 02:23.950
We need miso, salt, rice, and soy sauce.

02:23.950 --> 02:25.540
Oh, and vinegar, too.

02:25.540 --> 02:28.120
I will go with you after all, that I will.

02:28.120 --> 02:29.420
That's the spirit!

02:29.620 --> 02:32.380
Then let's head over with some vigor!

02:34.000 --> 02:34.840
Sir!

02:35.460 --> 02:38.920
It took longer than expected,
but I got the gist of it.

02:39.430 --> 02:43.640
The most popular around here
is the Chuetsu-ryu Maekawa Dojo.

02:44.050 --> 02:48.600
Its master, Kunai Maekawa, is likely
the most skilled in this area.

02:49.230 --> 02:50.100
Hmph.

02:50.310 --> 02:52.860
That, and the rurouni
that has recently started living

02:52.860 --> 02:56.320
in the Kamiya Kasshin-ryu Dojo
has rumors that he is ridiculously strong,

02:56.320 --> 02:59.650
but he's just a rurouni,
so he's likely nothing much.

03:00.150 --> 03:02.030
All right. Follow me.

03:02.030 --> 03:03.240
Yes, sir!

03:04.990 --> 03:07.330
CHUETSU-RYU
MAEKAWA DOJO

03:08.330 --> 03:09.290
Face!

03:13.420 --> 03:14.290
Hello!

03:14.500 --> 03:15.340
Oh!

03:15.460 --> 03:16.300
Oho!

03:16.840 --> 03:18.300
Hello, Miss Kaoru!

03:18.300 --> 03:19.130
Hello.

03:19.550 --> 03:20.970
We've been waiting for you.

03:20.970 --> 03:23.720
Don't worry about me.
Please continue your training.

03:24.220 --> 03:25.970
It's just like Kaoru says.

03:26.350 --> 03:28.430
Don't let this interrupt your training.

03:28.890 --> 03:29.980
Mr. Maekawa!

03:30.640 --> 03:35.560
I see. So you must be Kenshin
that Kaoru often talks about.

03:36.320 --> 03:38.690
Is that the rurouni
rumored to be really strong?

03:39.360 --> 03:40.360
Kenshin Himura.

03:41.110 --> 03:42.700
The man Mr. Maekawa mentioned

03:42.700 --> 03:45.120
he definitely wanted
to challenge at some point.

03:45.370 --> 03:48.120
If they do,
it will be a really tough challenge.

03:48.370 --> 03:50.830
The loser will not come out unscathed.

03:51.580 --> 03:55.040
<i>Mr. Maekawa never once mentioned
that to me.</i>

04:05.390 --> 04:06.220
Huh?

04:06.430 --> 04:07.850
Thank you for coming.

04:07.850 --> 04:09.680
Please, if you
could train everyone here...

04:09.680 --> 04:12.940
No, I just came as an escort
for Miss Kaoru, that I did.

04:12.940 --> 04:17.020
So I see. Then you should lounge
in the guest seat.

04:17.020 --> 04:18.150
Thank you so much.

04:22.280 --> 04:23.240
Sir...

04:24.200 --> 04:28.780
I'm sorry I didn't tell you. I felt
you'd never bring him if I told you.

04:28.990 --> 04:32.250
Don't worry.
I don't want to fight him anymore.

04:32.620 --> 04:36.880
No, to be precise,
I have lost even before fighting.

04:37.840 --> 04:41.920
So I see. A young man with good eyes.

04:42.550 --> 04:44.630
SIMPLE, STRONG SWORD

04:45.470 --> 04:48.100
Come on! Don't panic
each time someone gets really close!

04:48.430 --> 04:51.600
Don't back away. You have to squarely
look at your opponent's eyes first!

04:51.600 --> 04:52.430
Got that?

04:52.430 --> 04:53.560
Thank you very much.

04:54.060 --> 04:55.310
Okay, next!

04:56.310 --> 04:59.730
How is it, looking at our dojo?

05:00.730 --> 05:02.400
Looks good, that it does.

05:02.400 --> 05:04.950
You have a lot of students
and a lot of energy.

05:05.200 --> 05:08.620
Oh, I usually don't get
even one third of this.

05:09.120 --> 05:12.500
The rumored swordsmanship sweetheart
comes to help train.

05:12.500 --> 05:15.710
That seems to be charming entertainment
for the young ones.

05:16.460 --> 05:20.590
I'd say ten or less of them
take swordsmanship seriously.

05:21.090 --> 05:24.470
Sorry to say, this is
what has become of the great dojo

05:24.470 --> 05:28.140
said and proven to be best in town
back in the Edo period.

05:29.090 --> 05:32.180
That said,
the most pathetic part is myself,

05:32.180 --> 05:39.150
using the reminder of my sword-mate
Koshijiro Kamiya to attract students.

05:39.400 --> 05:42.480
No need to belittle yourself that much,
that is.

05:42.980 --> 05:45.570
It helps the Kamiya Dojo
as well in many ways

05:45.570 --> 05:47.860
with the lessons over here, that it does.

05:48.110 --> 05:50.780
It's give-and-take, that it is.

05:53.040 --> 05:57.370
However, what will become
of swordsmanship in the future?

05:58.170 --> 06:00.170
With the Meiji Revolution
and enlightenment,

06:00.170 --> 06:02.000
swordsmanship suddenly
went out of fashion.

06:02.000 --> 06:05.460
It definitely is heading down the path
of weakening and extinction.

06:06.220 --> 06:09.510
Having someone challenge the dojo
virtually every day in the past

06:09.510 --> 06:10.850
is so hard to believe.

06:14.350 --> 06:17.690
H-Hey! Don't come into the sacred dojo
with your shoes on!

06:17.690 --> 06:18.940
Take those zori sandals off!

06:19.600 --> 06:20.440
Get him!

06:23.320 --> 06:24.650
Damn you!

06:33.530 --> 06:37.620
I take it you are Kunai Maekawa,
founder of the Chuetsu-ryu.

06:38.250 --> 06:40.750
I would like to challenge you.

06:43.210 --> 06:45.500
I am Raijuta Isurugi!

06:46.010 --> 06:49.260
I am truly concerned
about the future of swordsmanship!

06:53.390 --> 06:55.850
<i>Cloudy eyes
that I cannot see deeply into...</i>

06:56.140 --> 06:57.560
<i>but he is strong!</i>

06:58.600 --> 07:00.310
I would like to challenge you!

07:00.480 --> 07:03.400
G-Go away! This dojo currently
doesn't spar with other styles—

07:03.400 --> 07:04.270
Hold it!

07:04.860 --> 07:07.030
Raijuta, was it?

07:07.030 --> 07:09.280
Fine, I will accept your challenge.

07:09.650 --> 07:12.200
Following usual rules,
we will do a best of three.

07:12.200 --> 07:14.620
The first to take two points
will be the winner.

07:15.740 --> 07:16.830
Is that all right?

07:17.040 --> 07:18.200
Mr. Maekawa.

07:18.200 --> 07:21.290
I understand. This is no ordinary man.

07:21.790 --> 07:24.500
That is why I am compelled to fight.

07:25.340 --> 07:26.670
Though I have aged,

07:26.670 --> 07:30.130
the name of Kunai Maekawa was
once included in Edo's best dozen.

07:30.130 --> 07:32.640
I will not go down that easily.

07:33.090 --> 07:34.350
A bamboo sword, huh.

07:36.060 --> 07:37.680
This is out of the question.

07:38.020 --> 07:39.020
What?

07:39.770 --> 07:40.810
Sir!

07:40.810 --> 07:42.900
You're late, Yutaro.

07:43.400 --> 07:44.610
There's nothing I could do.

07:44.940 --> 07:48.280
Between you and me, the lengths
of our strides are way too different.

07:48.530 --> 07:51.360
I ran here as fast as I could, you know.

07:51.990 --> 07:54.870
Anyways, the challenge,
real sword or wooden, which is it?

07:54.870 --> 07:56.080
Bamboo.

07:56.080 --> 07:56.910
Huh?

07:56.910 --> 07:59.330
Bamboo? A bamboo sword?

07:59.790 --> 08:02.040
A challenge with such a toy?

08:02.330 --> 08:04.880
So this was another dojo
that was a dojo in name only.

08:05.130 --> 08:06.290
Shut up!

08:07.040 --> 08:09.050
What are you doing, kiddo?

08:09.170 --> 08:11.010
No, you're the kiddo!

08:11.010 --> 08:12.050
You are, too.

08:12.380 --> 08:15.970
I'm the top student
of the Kamiya Kasshin-ryu, Yahiko Myojin!

08:15.970 --> 08:17.220
You better remember that!

08:17.220 --> 08:20.390
The top student of Sir Raijuta,
Yutaro Tsukayama!

08:20.390 --> 08:22.310
That kick will cost you dearly!

08:23.890 --> 08:24.980
Shut up.

08:25.600 --> 08:26.440
Hah!

08:27.690 --> 08:31.240
Unfortunately,
I have no such things as bamboo swords.

08:31.530 --> 08:33.200
I will borrow one.

08:34.160 --> 08:37.370
<i>It will be difficult for Mr. Maekawa
in his current state to win.</i>

08:37.870 --> 08:42.580
<i>It will likely end up at one win each,
and Raijuta will win the final point.</i>

08:44.120 --> 08:48.590
Then, to keep it fair, Kaoru Kamiya
will be the judge, as incompetent as I am,

08:48.590 --> 08:50.590
as I am of a differing style.

08:51.340 --> 08:54.930
Come. I will show you whether or not
this is out of the question.

08:56.590 --> 08:57.430
First match!

08:59.680 --> 09:01.100
Wh-What fighting spirit.

09:03.180 --> 09:06.230
You don't need to show me. I already know.

09:07.190 --> 09:09.770
With a best-of-three match
with bamboo swords,

09:09.770 --> 09:12.030
you are already out of the question!

09:12.030 --> 09:12.940
Oh, no!

09:20.950 --> 09:22.870
<i>I couldn't see him jumping in at all.</i>

09:23.370 --> 09:24.910
<i>What speed, despite his giant frame.</i>

09:26.000 --> 09:27.790
Did that Face not count?

09:28.960 --> 09:31.250
F-Face is valid! One point!

09:31.590 --> 09:33.010
Amazing.

09:33.010 --> 09:37.470
He missed, but that first swing down
was an amazing attack.

09:38.470 --> 09:40.220
He didn't miss with that one.

09:40.510 --> 09:43.390
For a blow to the head,
what you call Face,

09:43.390 --> 09:46.600
the blade sometimes slips
from the curve of the skull.

09:47.100 --> 09:49.310
So if you want to get a kill
by swinging down,

09:49.310 --> 09:51.190
you always aim for the collar.

09:51.190 --> 09:53.070
A fundamental aspect
of ancient sword arts.

09:54.610 --> 09:55.440
This isn't good!

09:55.990 --> 09:57.700
You have a fractured shoulder bone!

09:57.700 --> 09:59.410
- You need to hurry to a doctor!
- Wait!

09:59.910 --> 10:01.620
The match isn't over yet!

10:04.330 --> 10:06.330
Th-The second match.

10:11.380 --> 10:12.210
Second match!

10:14.460 --> 10:15.510
So pitiful!

10:15.510 --> 10:18.010
You are already dead
from the first attack!

10:19.890 --> 10:21.550
One point! Match over!

10:21.550 --> 10:22.390
That's enough!

10:23.600 --> 10:26.520
You fool who cannot even see
your own defeat...

10:28.390 --> 10:29.310
Hold it!

10:29.600 --> 10:30.600
What the...

10:38.650 --> 10:41.910
The match was already over
when you were the first to two points.

10:42.370 --> 10:43.990
Are you trying to kill, that you are?

10:44.620 --> 10:45.700
Indeed so.

10:47.040 --> 10:50.670
In the first place,
every man only has one life.

10:50.880 --> 10:53.670
And thus, every match only has one point.

10:54.460 --> 10:56.510
Either you take or be taken.

10:57.210 --> 10:59.930
Since the Edo period,
swordsmanship indeed flourished

10:59.930 --> 11:02.050
with the invention of the bamboo sword.

11:02.550 --> 11:03.930
However, because of that,

11:03.930 --> 11:07.140
the divine strengths seen
in ancient sword arts have been lost,

11:07.140 --> 11:08.980
and swordsmanship gets only weaker!

11:09.480 --> 11:11.350
These are times to lament!

11:11.350 --> 11:14.320
Fools who are rejoicing
at bamboo swordsmanship

11:14.690 --> 11:17.110
have no right to be wielding a sword!

11:20.070 --> 11:23.070
RUROUNI KENSHIN

11:23.820 --> 11:26.990
You don't belong to this dojo, do you?

11:27.580 --> 11:30.790
For now, I am under the care
of Kamiya Dojo, that I am.

11:31.000 --> 11:35.460
I see. So you're the skillful rurouni.

11:35.460 --> 11:36.750
Perfect timing.

11:36.750 --> 11:38.510
I challenge you to a match as well...

11:38.710 --> 11:40.220
with real blades.

11:42.680 --> 11:45.180
I do not intend on wielding a sword
for a trial of strength

11:45.180 --> 11:46.810
or to show off to others, that I don't.

11:47.390 --> 11:48.890
So I see.

11:49.180 --> 11:50.020
Yutaro.

11:50.020 --> 11:50.850
Yes?

11:51.140 --> 11:53.810
Take the dojo's sign down, and burn it.

11:54.520 --> 11:56.980
I was victorious
over the master of this dojo.

11:57.440 --> 12:00.490
I can do whatever I wish to the sign.

12:00.740 --> 12:02.950
If you are dissatisfied, bring it on.

12:03.570 --> 12:05.950
I will take all of you on together.

12:06.200 --> 12:09.450
I know! Why don't we burn it
out on the main street?

12:09.450 --> 12:10.540
That will be a flashier showing—

12:10.750 --> 12:12.410
That's enough.

12:13.330 --> 12:14.380
Let me go.

12:14.380 --> 12:15.380
You want to be killed?

12:18.840 --> 12:19.800
What's wrong?

12:20.300 --> 12:23.260
You're okay with me burning the sign?

12:23.840 --> 12:27.140
Hmph. Each and every one of you
is out of the question.

12:27.140 --> 12:28.220
Fine.

12:28.680 --> 12:29.930
I will take you on!

12:29.930 --> 12:30.930
Miss Kaoru!

12:31.520 --> 12:34.440
I don't go easy on women or children.

12:35.860 --> 12:36.690
All right.

12:37.480 --> 12:38.940
I will take you on.

12:39.860 --> 12:42.990
But this is nothing more
than sparring in a dojo.

12:42.990 --> 12:44.660
I refuse to use real blades.

12:44.910 --> 12:46.820
I'm not satisfied, but fine.

12:46.820 --> 12:49.830
Wooden sword, it is. First to one point.

12:54.460 --> 12:55.670
Is it okay?

12:55.670 --> 12:57.250
Yes, barely.

12:57.710 --> 12:58.960
Be careful.

12:58.960 --> 13:00.960
There's something about that man.

13:01.550 --> 13:02.880
I'm aware, that I am.

13:03.630 --> 13:04.630
Let's begin.

13:06.590 --> 13:07.600
A judge?

13:08.390 --> 13:09.640
No need.

13:14.020 --> 13:16.560
We finally get to see
just how strong that rurouni is.

13:16.770 --> 13:19.770
Yeah, but is he really that strong?

13:28.070 --> 13:31.660
That guy named Raijuta,
what speed and power when he swings down!

13:31.950 --> 13:33.620
And to easily dodge that,

13:33.620 --> 13:35.960
the rurouni is definitely
all that our master saw in him!

13:36.540 --> 13:40.130
<i>The attack and defense from both ends
are amazing, but, Kenshin...</i>

13:40.340 --> 13:41.880
<i>why aren't you swinging back?</i>

13:42.380 --> 13:43.210
<i>It can't be...</i>

13:44.470 --> 13:45.800
I see.

13:45.800 --> 13:50.970
If you manage to make it a draw,
I cannot do anything to the sign.

13:52.390 --> 13:54.230
Then, what about this?

13:55.770 --> 13:56.600
He's fast!

13:59.100 --> 14:00.270
What is this?

14:07.530 --> 14:09.660
You, what's your name?

14:09.990 --> 14:11.370
Kenshin Himura.

14:11.870 --> 14:13.290
I'll remember that.

14:14.790 --> 14:15.790
We're heading back.

14:15.790 --> 14:16.710
Huh?

14:16.710 --> 14:17.540
Oh, okay!

14:18.120 --> 14:21.460
I don't really get it,
but my master has the upper hand.

14:21.670 --> 14:23.460
Don't underestimate Kenshin.

14:23.460 --> 14:26.260
He hasn't even shown
half of his real strength yet.

14:27.550 --> 14:30.930
Looks like I'll have to settle the score
with you at some point.

14:33.430 --> 14:36.770
I'll beat you up,
so you just wait and see!

14:38.600 --> 14:39.600
Sheesh.

14:39.600 --> 14:41.520
He's a damn cheeky brat.

14:42.900 --> 14:46.030
What was that about
not even half of his real strength?

14:46.030 --> 14:47.650
He's such a bad loser.

14:48.400 --> 14:50.660
Kenshin... Himura.

14:50.660 --> 14:51.620
Sir?

14:53.370 --> 14:57.540
<i>My Secret Sword: Izuna
has never been dodged before.</i>

14:58.040 --> 15:00.620
<i>That man is likely a fellow user
of an ancient sword art</i>

15:00.620 --> 15:03.090
<i>and quite a skilled user at that.</i>

15:03.340 --> 15:07.090
<i>Kenshin Himura.
I have no complaints about his strength!</i>

15:08.010 --> 15:10.510
Amazing. What the heck is this?

15:10.510 --> 15:13.140
It's as if a real blade
was slammed down here.

15:16.140 --> 15:17.730
<i>This isn't just a real blade.</i>

15:19.190 --> 15:22.940
<i>Something even sharper
has done the slicing.</i>

15:23.400 --> 15:26.110
<i>This isn't a technique
used by an ordinary dojo challenger.</i>

15:27.150 --> 15:31.200
Raijuta Isurugi,
what in the world are you, that you are?

15:32.620 --> 15:34.870
KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO

15:33.620 --> 15:34.870
I see.

15:35.410 --> 15:39.290
Someone that fun
showed up on a day I didn't drop by?

15:39.290 --> 15:40.750
Not fun!

15:40.870 --> 15:45.130
Because of that guy, Maekawa Dojo
is closing down for a while!

15:46.050 --> 15:47.130
Hmm.

15:47.300 --> 15:50.220
The match itself was done properly, right?

15:50.220 --> 15:52.300
And it was just a one-sided battle.

15:52.300 --> 15:53.140
But—

15:53.140 --> 15:55.550
If you're in charge of a style and a dojo,

15:55.550 --> 15:58.520
"The opponent was too strong"
won't be a valid excuse.

15:59.020 --> 16:00.680
Right, Kenshin?

16:01.600 --> 16:03.600
That is indeed true, that it is.

16:04.310 --> 16:05.770
<i>But in any case...</i>

16:05.770 --> 16:10.030
<i>what is someone who doesn't care
at all for bamboo swordsmanship</i>

16:10.030 --> 16:13.110
<i>and focused on actual battles
doing by challenging dojos?</i>

16:14.030 --> 16:15.530
Excuse me.

16:15.950 --> 16:19.580
Does Mr. Kenshin Himura reside here?

16:19.910 --> 16:21.960
I am Himura, that I am.

16:23.620 --> 16:26.920
INVITATION

16:24.290 --> 16:26.380
I was entrusted with this.

16:29.630 --> 16:31.260
RAIJUTA ISURUGI

16:30.260 --> 16:32.590
What is this? What does this mean?

16:31.260 --> 16:34.720
INVITATION

16:32.590 --> 16:35.180
Doesn't it mean a challenge for a duel?

16:35.180 --> 16:38.260
Well, I am nothing more than a butler.

16:38.640 --> 16:42.520
Anyway, please board the carriage
waiting outside. Now, go on.

16:45.440 --> 16:47.190
Please, this way.

16:47.400 --> 16:50.360
The main mansion is past the garden.

16:52.700 --> 16:54.110
You must be Mr. Himura.

16:54.530 --> 16:55.780
Nice to meet you.

16:55.780 --> 16:57.580
I am the master of this house.

16:57.780 --> 17:00.290
My name is Yuzaemon Tsukayama.

17:00.490 --> 17:01.660
Tsukayama?

17:02.120 --> 17:04.250
Can you possibly be that damn brat's dad?

17:04.460 --> 17:06.170
Damn brat? How rude!

17:06.580 --> 17:09.210
Sir Raijuta only called for Himura!

17:09.210 --> 17:10.300
Why are you here?

17:10.300 --> 17:11.550
Stop that, Yutaro!

17:12.090 --> 17:14.170
They are companions
of the master's guests.

17:14.170 --> 17:16.140
I will not allow you to be disrespectful!

17:16.140 --> 17:16.970
Hmph!

17:17.300 --> 17:21.430
I am terribly sorry for the disrespect
my son has shown you.

17:21.430 --> 17:22.350
It's nothing.

17:22.680 --> 17:25.350
The master is at the lakeside.

17:25.350 --> 17:27.060
I will guide you there.

17:27.350 --> 17:28.730
Now, this way.

17:31.280 --> 17:35.450
Yutaro, you should entertain
all the companions.

17:38.530 --> 17:39.490
Guess I got no choice.

17:39.490 --> 17:42.700
I can at least serve some pickles
made with sake lees and second-flush tea.

17:42.700 --> 17:45.460
Oh? That's quite a serving there.

17:45.870 --> 17:50.000
But sorry to tell you.
We're gonna have to pass.

17:50.130 --> 17:50.960
Huh?

17:52.590 --> 17:55.880
I am involved in the export of swords.

17:55.880 --> 17:59.180
In Europe, Japanese swords
are treated as pieces of art

17:59.180 --> 18:00.970
and have high selling prices.

18:01.260 --> 18:06.230
That's why I was attacked by bandits
about three months ago, carriage and all.

18:06.440 --> 18:09.480
Our master passed by just then
and saved me.

18:09.480 --> 18:12.980
Yutaro has completely
come to admire his strength

18:12.980 --> 18:14.820
and wishes to train under him.

18:15.400 --> 18:20.530
That's why he has been here at our place
as a swordsmanship instructor.

18:21.990 --> 18:22.910
Sir.

18:24.540 --> 18:26.160
Now, take your time.

18:31.340 --> 18:34.130
Hmph. So that's Raijuta?

18:34.380 --> 18:37.470
That aside, are we okay
doing that kind of stuff?

18:37.470 --> 18:39.590
I don't care about guys like him.

18:43.260 --> 18:45.220
What do you want from me, that you do?

18:46.060 --> 18:49.270
How do you think
swordsmanship should be today?

18:49.520 --> 18:51.730
Don't you think it is spineless?

18:52.110 --> 18:54.900
Don't you feel it is scant
and too delicate?

18:55.820 --> 18:58.450
The weak are always culled.

18:59.030 --> 19:01.410
That is the law of nature.

19:04.030 --> 19:06.370
My style is Shinko-ryu.

19:06.370 --> 19:11.000
I seek to fulfill the great deed of
restoring swordsmanship in its name.

19:11.290 --> 19:15.000
Why is someone with such grandiose plans
challenging dojos?

19:15.590 --> 19:21.140
My desire is the eradication
of the over 500 swordsmanship styles.

19:22.430 --> 19:23.720
It's not restoration?

19:24.220 --> 19:25.890
It is restoration.

19:25.890 --> 19:30.350
But before that, it is essential
to remove all the incompetent ones.

19:30.980 --> 19:33.900
I will first crush
all of the bamboo swordsmanship,

19:33.900 --> 19:37.110
the root of the weakening
of today's swordsmanship!

19:38.280 --> 19:41.280
And afterwards, my Shinko-ryu will be

19:41.280 --> 19:44.870
the one and only authentic swordsmanship
style as I begin the restoration.

19:45.080 --> 19:47.290
I aim to have
an invincible swordsmanship style

19:47.290 --> 19:49.870
that holds its own
against Western heavy weapons.

19:50.080 --> 19:51.120
What is he...

19:51.620 --> 19:53.000
<i>I see.</i>

19:53.000 --> 19:55.880
<i>By allowing only a select few
to inherit swordsmanship skills,</i>

19:55.880 --> 19:58.590
<i>he'll preserve the purity of its strength.</i>

19:58.920 --> 20:02.640
You are a man capable
of dodging Secret Sword: Izuna.

20:03.140 --> 20:05.350
Lend a hand to this grand ambition.

20:06.560 --> 20:08.600
Ancient sword arts
are all murderous swords,

20:08.600 --> 20:09.810
focused on actual battles.

20:10.560 --> 20:13.060
Are you saying that
being aware of this, that you are?

20:13.270 --> 20:18.820
Of course. The current mainstream
of bamboo swordsmanship is the fake one.

20:19.320 --> 20:20.280
So I see.

20:21.820 --> 20:25.950
In that case, you and I don't get along
with each other, that we don't.

20:27.240 --> 20:29.330
You think nothing of it,
even if swordsmanship

20:29.330 --> 20:31.250
will fall to ruin
unless something is done?

20:32.670 --> 20:35.040
I am a swordsman myself,
even if not much of one.

20:35.380 --> 20:38.000
I do have feelings
of lamenting the future of swordsmanship.

20:38.750 --> 20:42.550
However, if the future is one
where murderous swords thrive,

20:42.550 --> 20:43.970
I would gladly decline.

20:44.720 --> 20:48.060
I will not deny that the basic nature
of swordsmanship is murder.

20:48.060 --> 20:52.890
However, if it means oppressing others
and trying to crush life-giving swords...

20:53.440 --> 20:56.610
I will use all of my strength to stop you.

20:58.860 --> 21:00.190
I see.

21:00.650 --> 21:03.860
So you are not in agreement
to my grand plan.

21:07.620 --> 21:11.120
Then, as of this moment, you are an enemy!

22:45.090 --> 22:50.090
NEXT EPISODE
THE IDEAL MAN

22:46.590 --> 22:49.090
<i>Next episode, "The Ideal Man."</i>
